{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. I understand you had a fall in clinic today and your blood sugar was very high. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:15:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been feeling weak and dizzy. My sugars have been in the 500s before meals. I haven’t been eating much. And my left foot feels numb, so I tripped over the IV tubing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’re on chemotherapy for multiple myeloma, correct? And you were off your long-acting insulin for a few months?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:18:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I was on glargine, but my doctor stopped it because my sugars were good. But since starting this new chemo, they’ve gone way up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:19:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Chemotherapy like dexamethasone can raise blood sugar. We’ll restart your glargine and adjust your sliding scale insulin to get it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I’m worried about falling again. My left leg feels weak and numb."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve ordered a CT of your head to make sure there’s no injury from the fall. We’ll also check your neuropathy. You have a history of a T12 fracture—has that been painful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really painful, but I feel unsteady. And my left knee is arthritic too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:25:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep an eye on that. Your labs show low platelets and white blood cells, which could be from your myeloma or the chemo. You received a platelet transfusion in clinic—do you know why it was needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:26:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my counts have been low. I was on Bactrim, but my doctor said it might be affecting my marrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:28:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to atovaquone to reduce that risk. We also held your anticoagulant because of the low platelets. We’ll restart it once your counts improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:29:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a pulmonary embolism before—should I be worried about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are monitoring that. For now, safety comes first with your platelet count. We’ll follow your labs closely and restart anticoagulation as soon as it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. What about my blood pressure? It’s usually high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:33:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your BP is stable. We’ve kept you on labetalol and stopped amlodipine to simplify things. We’ll continue monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my hepatitis B? I’m on lamivudine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re still on lamivudine daily. We’ll continue that. We just got your viral load back—HBV DNA is not detected, which is excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. And HCV?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:39:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also negative. No detectable HCV RNA. So your liver meds are working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:40:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been tired and nauseated too, but no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-11-06 22:41:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be from the chemo or your myeloma. We’ll keep you on dexamethasone and gabapentin for the neuropathy. We’ll also give you fluids to help with your intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT head was normal—no bleeding or injury. Your chest X-ray was also clear. We’re not concerned about a new lung issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any update on my blood sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we restarted glargine at 25 units at bedtime and adjusted your sliding scale. Your glucose this morning was 134—much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:19:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about the falls? Is it just the neuropathy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:20:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s a combination—high sugars can cause dizziness, and your neuropathy affects balance. We’ve scheduled a physical therapy consult to assess your gait."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need a walker?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:23:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. PT will recommend what’s safest. We also ordered an MRI of your spine to check your old T12 fracture and see if there’s any new nerve compression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:24:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I remember that fracture. It was from the myeloma, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:26:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a pathologic fracture. The MRI will show if it’s stable or if there’s progression. Your myeloma is relapsing—we saw your bone marrow biopsy showed 70% plasma cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:27:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the chemo is still needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll restart your RVD regimen—Revlimid, Velcade, and dexamethasone. You’re in cycle 2. We’ll give Velcade tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:30:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will that affect my blood counts more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-11-07 08:31:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might. That’s why we’re monitoring closely and gave you a platelet transfusion. We’ll check your labs daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your MRI results are back. The T12 fracture is stable—no new collapse or spinal cord issues. But you do have severe narrowing at L5-S1 on the right side, which could contribute to your left foot numbness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why my foot feels so bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:02:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. The degenerative changes are long-standing. We’ll keep you on gabapentin and refer you to ortho for your knee, but no surgery is urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:04:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get your Velcade injection today. We’ve adjusted the dose based on your weight. Any questions before we proceed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:06:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I trust the plan. Just want to stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:08:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aiming for that. Your sugars are staying in the 130s—great job. We’ll keep you on 30 units of glargine at bedtime now that we’ve titrated up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:09:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need insulin when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-11-08 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re sending you home with glargine and your sliding scale. You have an appointment with your endocrinologist next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. Platelets still low at 26, so we gave another unit yesterday. We’ll check again today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any sign of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:32:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. Your blood cultures are negative, and you’re not febrile. The chronic ear issue on the CT is old—no treatment needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:34:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my liver? The AST and ALT were up a bit yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mild elevation—likely from the chemo or your condition. No signs of hepatitis flare. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:38:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your platelets stay stable and you remain safe walking, we’re planning for discharge tomorrow. PT cleared you to use a rolling walker at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:39:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll need help at first?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-11-09 08:41:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, home health will send a nurse and therapist. You’ll need to follow up with your oncologist, endocrinologist, and primary doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your labs are stable, and you’ve done well. We’re discharging you home with services."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What medications am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:02:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds: Revlimid, Velcade on schedule, glargine at night, gabapentin, omeprazole, and the others. Plus atovaquone instead of Bactrim."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:04:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the insulin sliding scale?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue as directed. Check your sugars four times a day. Call your endocrinologist if they’re over 250 consistently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:06:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I restart blood thinners?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:08:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your oncologist will decide once your platelets are above 50. Don’t restart without checking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my next chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:10:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with your oncology team—they’ll schedule your next Velcade dose. Keep using the rolling walker and take your time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:12:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything changes—especially dizziness, falls, or high sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:14:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:16:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge nurse will go over your instructions and medications in detail before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready when she is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2174-11-10 09:18:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re glad we could help. Stay safe and keep in touch with your team."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-11-06 22:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-11-10 17:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted due to hyperglycemia and mechanical falls in the setting of multiple myeloma and chemotherapy. He presented with blood glucose levels in the 500s, poor oral intake, and worsening peripheral neuropathy leading to multiple falls. His long-acting insulin had been discontinued months prior, contributing to poor glycemic control. He received a platelet transfusion for thrombocytopenia and was restarted on glargine insulin with improved glucose levels. A CT head and chest X-ray showed no acute abnormalities. MRI of the spine revealed a stable T12 compression fracture and degenerative changes without cord compression. He received Velcade chemotherapy during admission. His anticoagulation was held due to low platelets and to be resumed outpatient. He was discharged home with a rolling walker, home health services, and follow-up appointments with his oncologist, endocrinologist, and primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced pancytopenia",
      "Multiple myeloma, in relapse",
      "Other pancytopenia",
      "Peripheral stem cells replaced by transplant",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without mention of hepatic coma without mention of hepatitis delta",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified sleep apnea",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Sickle-cell trait",
